{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656180",
      "title": "Binding to Directive Properties",
      "lectureOrder": 422,
      "videoOrder": 388,
      "sourceHash": "310920d84aa88606e1da1552cb353ecfaf40e7d10eb23803a3a951fce5bebd81",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.49,
          "end": 5.19,
          "en": "-: Our directive is looking really great.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.19,
          "end": 6.33,
          "en": "We're almost there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.33,
          "end": 9.45,
          "en": "but there's one other thing I want to add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.45,
          "end": 13.08,
          "en": "One functionality I want to add, right now it's dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.08,
          "end": 14.46,
          "en": "in a way that we can mouse",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.46,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "over and then move the mouse away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 20.25,
          "en": "but we can't decide which colors get used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.25,
          "end": 23.67,
          "en": "Now if that were a directive, we want to ship with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.67,
          "end": 27.12,
          "en": "let's say a third party package, we're offering the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.12,
          "end": 29.34,
          "en": "the developer using this directive should be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.34,
          "end": 31.8,
          "en": "able to dynamically set the value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.8,
          "end": 33.96,
          "en": "Maybe we even want to do this in our own app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.96,
          "end": 37.29,
          "en": "because the color we want to set changes depending",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.29,
          "end": 39.75,
          "en": "on some our parameters in our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.75,
          "end": 42.15,
          "en": "Right now, the color is hard coded in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.15,
          "end": 45.78,
          "en": "transparent by default and blue if mouse over it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.78,
          "end": 48.24,
          "en": "So that is something we can improve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.24,
          "end": 51.3,
          "en": "and we can improve it with a tool we already learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.3,
          "end": 53.91,
          "en": "Custom property binding as a side note",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.91,
          "end": 56.73,
          "en": "custom event binding all the works and directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.73,
          "end": 59.64,
          "en": "but you probably won't use that that often.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.64,
          "end": 63.363,
          "en": "So how can we use custom property binding then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.26,
          "end": 67.65,
          "en": "Let's add two properties to which we bind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.65,
          "end": 72.65,
          "en": "I'll add it with input here and I'll name the first one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.78,
          "end": 77.31,
          "en": "default color and set it equal to a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.31,
          "end": 80.82300000000001,
          "en": "and even assign a default color, which is transparent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.56,
          "end": 84.09,
          "en": "Now add input of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.09,
          "end": 87.36,
          "en": "needs to be imported from at angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.36,
          "end": 92.36,
          "en": "I'll duplicate this and I'll set this to highlight color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.49000000000001,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "That will be blue by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 96.87,
          "en": "So we do have some default values to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.87,
          "end": 99.723,
          "en": "but they can be overwritten from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.56,
          "end": 104.993,
          "en": "So now by default here I will assign my highlight color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.1,
          "end": 108.90299999999999,
          "en": "for initially setting this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.97999999999999,
          "end": 114.87,
          "en": "And in my host listeners here, if I mouse over it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.87,
          "end": 117.42,
          "en": "I will assign my highlight color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.42,
          "end": 119.7,
          "en": "Excuse me here, it should be my default color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.7,
          "end": 120.69,
          "en": "at the top of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.69,
          "end": 123.72,
          "en": "So default color, color when we initialize this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.72,
          "end": 127.65,
          "en": "and then highlight color once we mouse over this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.65,
          "end": 130.89,
          "en": "And then default color again once we move the mouse away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.89,
          "end": 132.603,
          "en": "So here, default color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.47,
          "end": 134.97,
          "en": "So with this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.97,
          "end": 138.87,
          "en": "it should still work just the way as it did before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.87,
          "end": 142.95,
          "en": "but now we can actually bind this from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.95,
          "end": 144.45,
          "en": "So in our app component where we use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.45,
          "end": 147.27,
          "en": "the better highlight directive, we can now bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.27,
          "end": 151.05,
          "en": "to default color and maybe set this to yellow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.05,
          "end": 154.07999999999998,
          "en": "Should be a string though yellow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.07999999999998,
          "end": 156.75,
          "en": "And we can bind to highlight color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.75,
          "end": 159.66,
          "en": "and pass a string, which could be red.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.66,
          "end": 161.13,
          "en": "And now if we save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.13,
          "end": 164.37,
          "en": "notice that app better highlight the directives itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.37,
          "end": 167.79,
          "en": "The name is not enclosed in square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.79,
          "end": 170.61,
          "en": "Now you'll see it's red and yellow here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.61,
          "end": 173.76,
          "en": "Though we also detect a black initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.76,
          "end": 176.04,
          "en": "before we mouse over, it's a white.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.04,
          "end": 179.61,
          "en": "The reason for this is when we assign default color here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.61,
          "end": 181.77,
          "en": "it's just not set here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.77,
          "end": 185.1,
          "en": "So to prevent this from happening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.1,
          "end": 187.8,
          "en": "what we can simply do is we initialize it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.8,
          "end": 189.24,
          "en": "in ngOnInit stat.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.24,
          "end": 191.61,
          "en": "That's all the before anything has been rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.61,
          "end": 195.083,
          "en": "But after our values here are available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.083,
          "end": 199.07999999999998,
          "en": "so here we can set this background color to this default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.07999999999998,
          "end": 202.02,
          "en": "this default color, and now it should work fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.02,
          "end": 204.06,
          "en": "Now we have yellow by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 204.06,
          "end": 207.75,
          "en": "so this now works and now we are able to override this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.75,
          "end": 209.85,
          "en": "There are a couple of interesting things we can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.85,
          "end": 213.633,
          "en": "observe regarding the way we pass down these values though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214.62,
          "end": 216.57,
          "en": "The first interesting thing is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 216.57,
          "end": 221.57,
          "en": "that we have two extra directive like looking things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.73,
          "end": 225.36,
          "en": "on the paragraph and this is just property binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 225.36,
          "end": 227.13,
          "en": "Now how does angular know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 227.13,
          "end": 230.28,
          "en": "if we want to bind to a property of paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 230.28,
          "end": 232.98,
          "en": "which of course doesn't have a default color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 232.98,
          "end": 235.65,
          "en": "or to a property of our directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 235.65,
          "end": 238.05,
          "en": "the answer is it just figures that out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 238.05,
          "end": 240.48,
          "en": "It simply checks our own directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 240.48,
          "end": 243.45,
          "en": "and so on first before it reaches the custom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.45,
          "end": 245.61,
          "en": "the native properties of elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 245.61,
          "end": 247.59,
          "en": "That's another important takeaway.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 247.59,
          "end": 250.95,
          "en": "We can bind to properties of our own directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 250.95,
          "end": 253.2,
          "en": "by simply placing them on the same element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 253.2,
          "end": 255.66,
          "en": "These properties, I mean enclosed in square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 255.66,
          "end": 257.16,
          "en": "of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 257.16,
          "end": 259.68,
          "en": "Now for NG class you see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 259.68,
          "end": 262.59,
          "en": "that somehow the directive itself is enclosed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 262.59,
          "end": 265.35,
          "en": "at square brackets and that's a typical use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 265.35,
          "end": 268.32,
          "en": "especially if you only have one property to bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 268.32,
          "end": 271.02,
          "en": "or at least one main property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 271.02,
          "end": 273.42,
          "en": "Then you can provide an alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 273.42,
          "end": 278.1,
          "en": "and we can do this here for let's say the highlight color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 278.1,
          "end": 281.46,
          "en": "and set this equal to your directive selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 281.46,
          "end": 284.07,
          "en": "So app better highlight in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 284.07,
          "end": 288.72,
          "en": "if I set this as an alias for the highlight color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 288.72,
          "end": 292.02,
          "en": "now this assignment here won't work anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 292.02,
          "end": 294.78,
          "en": "so I will remove it instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 294.78,
          "end": 297.09000000000003,
          "en": "now I can enclose my main directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 297.09000000000003,
          "end": 301.38,
          "en": "into square brackets and set this equal to red.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 301.38,
          "end": 304.18,
          "en": "So now we should still see yellow and red",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 305.13,
          "end": 307.2,
          "en": "but now we are having the same style",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 307.2,
          "end": 309.54,
          "en": "of and closing the directive itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 309.54,
          "end": 311.97,
          "en": "And it's important to understand that this is only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 311.97,
          "end": 313.05,
          "en": "an option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 313.05,
          "end": 317.34,
          "en": "You can set such a such an alias but that's not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 317.34,
          "end": 319.11,
          "en": "something you have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 319.11,
          "end": 323.34,
          "en": "And by default, as you saw before, the directive name is not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 323.34,
          "end": 324.72,
          "en": "enclosed in squared brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 324.72,
          "end": 327.66,
          "en": "That really only happens if you want to bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 327.66,
          "end": 331.5,
          "en": "to a property which has the same name or alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 331.5,
          "end": 333.963,
          "en": "like your directive selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 335.25,
          "end": 337.77,
          "en": "One other thing about how we pass down data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 337.77,
          "end": 341.37,
          "en": "One other thing which is true about property binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 341.37,
          "end": 346.37,
          "en": "in general, if you pass down a string like now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 346.44,
          "end": 350.73,
          "en": "we use square brackets and then single quotation marks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 350.73,
          "end": 353.1,
          "en": "While you can take a shortcut, you can remove",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 353.1,
          "end": 356.1,
          "en": "the square brackets and remove the single quotation marks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 356.1,
          "end": 357.81,
          "en": "And that is a special case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 357.81,
          "end": 360.48,
          "en": "If you are passing down a string, you can do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 360.48,
          "end": 364.17,
          "en": "you can add property binding without square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 364.17,
          "end": 366.93,
          "en": "If you then also omit these single quotation marks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 366.93,
          "end": 368.85,
          "en": "between the double quotation marks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 368.85,
          "end": 372.66,
          "en": "and that should work as it did before, no error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 372.66,
          "end": 375.15,
          "en": "You can use this, you will see me use this later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 375.15,
          "end": 378.66,
          "en": "in the course with official angular directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 378.66,
          "end": 381.57,
          "en": "Be careful that if you use it, it's really clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 381.57,
          "end": 384.54,
          "en": "that this is property binding, that no one thinks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 384.54,
          "end": 387.39,
          "en": "that this could be a real attribute existing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 387.39,
          "end": 389.37,
          "en": "for the element you placed it on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 389.37,
          "end": 392.04,
          "en": "Then this is absolutely fine to be used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 392.04,
          "end": 394.74,
          "en": "And this is our directive finished",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 394.74,
          "end": 396.9,
          "en": "with some extra features like host listener,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 396.9,
          "end": 401.253,
          "en": "host binding, and dynamically setting values from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
